description:
A compact pill for tags, attributes, filters and removable tokens, in Button's palette.

  Chip { "Design" }
  Chip(variant: :primary, size: :sm) { Icon(:circle_check, data: { icon: "start" }); plain "Verified" }
  Chip(dismissible: true, close_label: "Remove React") { "React" }
  Chip(href: "/tags/design") { "#design" }

It's a <button> (an <a> with `href:`). `dismissible: true` adds a ✕: clicking the chip plays an exit animation, removes it and emits `ui--chip:dismiss` (cancel it to keep the chip - e.g. to remove it with a Turbo Stream instead). Inside a ChipGroup it takes the group's variant and size.

ChipCheckbox.description:
A Chip you can select: a <label> in Chip's look around a visually hidden checkbox, so a set of them submits like check boxes. The checked chip turns primary and shows a check - pure CSS.

  ChipGroup(variant: :outline, role: "group", aria_label: "Tags") do
    ChipCheckbox(name: "tags[]", value: "ruby", checked: true) { "Ruby" }
    ChipCheckbox(name: "tags[]", value: "rails") { "Rails" }
  end

Inside a ChipGroup it takes the group's variant and size (outline by default).

examples.code:
phlex do
  div(class: "flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2") do
    Chip(variant: :soft) { Icon(:plus, data: { icon: "start" }); plain "New" }
    Chip(variant: :primary) { Icon(:circle_check, data: { icon: "start" }); plain "Verified" }
    Chip(variant: :outline) { plain "4.9"; Icon(:star, data: { icon: "end" }) }
  end
end

phlex do
  div(class: "flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2") do
    Chip(href: "#design") { "#design" }
    Chip(href: "#engineering") { "#engineering" }
    Chip(href: "#featured", variant: :primary) { "#featured" }
  end
end
